glib 2.88.4, Windows: the revert of upstream 5a3231dbd ("GIO/Win32: Remove
custom definitions of system interfaces", 2025-07-29, first released in 2.87).

That commit dropped glib's own gio/gwin32api-*.h and made gio include the
WinRT headers windows.storage.h, windows.applicationmodel.core.h and
windows.management.deployment.h from the toolchain. The windows-x86_64
toolchain (Ubuntu 24.04's mingw-w64 11.0.1) has none of them, and gio stops
at gwin32packageparser.c. This restores the five headers and the two files
as they were. The code is the UWP package parser behind GAppInfo on Windows,
which neither librsvg nor FFmpeg calls; the rest of glib stays 2.88.4, which
is the point: 2.88.3/2.88.4 fix CVE-2026-15588 and CVE-2026-16118, which no
2.86 release does.

scripts/50-librsvg.sh applies it only when the compiler cannot find
windows.applicationmodel.core.h (windows-aarch64's llvm-mingw has it). Drop
it when the x86_64 toolchain has the WinRT headers.

